description:
Add ETag-based HTTP caching for GitHub API GET requests to reduce rate limit consumption. Cache responses and use If-None-Match headers on subsequent requests.

## what changes

### packages/plot/src/tracker/github/
- wrap Octokit with a request hook that caches GET responses by ETag
- on subsequent requests, send If-None-Match header
- on 304 Not Modified, return cached response
- cache key: method + url + accept header

## pattern (from lalph)

```typescript
octokit.hook.wrap("request", async (request, options) => {
  if (requestMethod(options) !== "GET") return request(options)
  const key = requestCacheKey(options)
  const cached = etagCache.get(key)
  const headers = cached
    ? { ...options.headers, "if-none-match": cached.etag }
    : options.headers
  try {
    const response = await request({ ...options, headers })
    const etag = etagHeaderValue(response.headers)
    if (etag) etagCache.set(key, { etag, data: response.data, ... })
    return response
  } catch (cause) {
    if (isNotModifiedError(cause) && cached) {
      return { status: 200, headers: cached.headers, data: cached.data, ... }
    }
    throw cause
  }
})
```

## reference
- lalph: src/Github.ts lines 73-114 (etag caching hook)
- repo: https://github.com/tim-smart/lalph

## verification
- `bun run typecheck` passes
- github API polling uses fewer API calls
- 304 responses correctly return cached data

Replace bare `Effect.gen(function* () { ... })` closures with `Effect.fnUntraced` throughout plot and sdk packages where appropriate.

## what changes
- effectful functions that take parameters should use `Effect.fnUntraced`
- keep `Effect.gen` for top-level service constructors and simple inline effects
- applies to: packages/plot/src, packages/sdk/src

## pattern

```typescript
// before
const doThing = (options: Options) =>
  Effect.gen(function* () {
    // ...
  })

// after
const doThing = Effect.fnUntraced(function* (options: Options) {
  // ...
})
```

## reference
- lalph uses this pervasively: src/Github.ts, src/Worktree.ts, src/Prd.ts
- repo: https://github.com/tim-smart/lalph

